```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Transfer {
    pub from: String,
    pub to: String,
    pub units: u64,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Record {
    pub transfer: Transfer,
    pub sequence: u64,
    pub previous_digest: u64,
    pub digest: u64,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]
pub struct TransferLog {
    pub records: Vec<Record>,
}

pub fn record_digest(transfer: &Transfer, sequence: u64, previous_digest: u64) -> u64;

impl TransferLog {
    pub fn new() -> Self;
    pub fn append(&mut self, transfer: Transfer) -> Result<u64, &'static str>;
    pub fn is_valid(&self) -> bool;
}
```

`record_digest` must be deterministic: start with FNV-1a 64-bit offset `14695981039346656037`; feed the bytes of `from`, then one zero byte, `to`, one zero byte, `units.to_le_bytes()`, `sequence.to_le_bytes()`, and `previous_digest.to_le_bytes()`. For each byte, XOR then multiply by `1099511628211` with wrapping arithmetic.

`append` rejects an empty sender, empty receiver, or a log whose length cannot be represented as `u64`, without mutation. Sequence numbers start at zero. The first previous digest is zero; later records use the stored digest of the preceding record. Return the new digest. `is_valid` accepts an empty log and verifies every sequence, link, and recomputed digest without mutation. Public fields may be deliberately altered, and validation must detect it. Do not include `main`.

